---
// Standalone page — deliberately does NOT use ../layouts/BlogPost.astro.
// This is CardProAI's privacy policy (an unrelated hobby card-reselling
// tool), hosted here only because eBay's developer platform requires a
// non-eBay URL for its OAuth app setup. Not a CFTrust page — no shared
// header/footer/nav, not linked from anywhere on cftrust.org, excluded
// from the sitemap (see astro.config.mjs). Christian, 2026-09-06.
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="UTF-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
	<meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
	<title>CardProAI Privacy Policy</title>
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
	<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
	<style>
		:root {
			--bg: #0d1117;
			--surface: #161b22;
			--border: #30363d;
			--text: #c9d1d9;
			--muted: #8b949e;
			--accent: #58a6ff;
			--accent-dim: #1f3a5f;
		}
		* { box-sizing: border-box; }
		body {
			margin: 0;
			background: var(--bg);
			color: var(--text);
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Sans', -apple-system, sans-serif;
			line-height: 1.65;
		}
		.wrap {
			max-width: 680px;
			margin: 0 auto;
			padding: 64px 24px 80px;
		}
		.eyebrow {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.78rem;
			letter-spacing: 0.08em;
			text-transform: uppercase;
			color: var(--accent);
			margin: 0 0 10px;
		}
		h1 {
			font-size: 2rem;
			font-weight: 700;
			margin: 0 0 6px;
			text-wrap: balance;
		}
		.meta {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.82rem;
			color: var(--muted);
			margin: 0 0 40px;
			display: flex;
			gap: 18px;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
		}
		.meta span { white-space: nowrap; }
		section {
			border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
			padding: 28px 0;
		}
		section:last-of-type { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
		h2 {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
			font-weight: 600;
			margin: 0 0 14px;
			display: flex;
			align-items: baseline;
			gap: 10px;
		}
		h2 .num {
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.85rem;
			color: var(--accent);
			font-weight: 500;
		}
		p { margin: 0 0 12px; max-width: 62ch; }
		p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
		ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 22px; max-width: 62ch; }
		li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
		strong { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; }
		.contact {
			margin-top: 40px;
			background: var(--surface);
			border: 1px solid var(--border);
			border-radius: 8px;
			padding: 18px 20px;
			font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
			font-size: 0.88rem;
		}
		.contact .label { color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; margin-bottom: 4px; }
		.contact a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
		.contact a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</p>
		<h1>CardProAI</h1>
		<p class="meta">
			<span>Effective 2026-09-06</span>
			<span>Single-operator hobby tool</span>
		</p>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">1</span>What this is</h2>
			<p>
				CardProAI is a personal inventory and listing tool built and operated
				by one individual for their own sports-card reselling hobby. It is not
				a public service, does not have user accounts, and does not process
				data on behalf of any third party. It connects to the operator's own
				eBay seller account, using eBay's own APIs under an authorization the
				operator grants themselves, to help create and manage the operator's
				own eBay listings.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">2</span>Information we access</h2>
			<p>Limited strictly to the operator's own eBay seller account, and only what's needed to build listings:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Inventory and listing data the operator creates (item titles, prices, photos, quantities)</li>
				<li>The operator's existing eBay business policies (payment, return, and shipping/fulfillment) and merchant inventory location, so new listings can reference them</li>
			</ul>
			<p>No data belonging to eBay buyers, other sellers, or any third party is ever accessed.</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">3</span>What we do not collect</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>No account registration, no cookies, no visitor tracking or analytics on this page</li>
				<li>No data from eBay buyers or any other eBay user</li>
				<li>No data is sold, rented, or shared with advertisers or any third party</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">4</span>How information is used</h2>
			<p>
				Solely to build and manage listing drafts on the operator's own eBay
				seller account. Every listing created is saved as a draft for the
				operator to review — nothing is published or activated automatically.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">5</span>Data storage &amp; security</h2>
			<p>
				All data stays on infrastructure the operator personally owns and
				controls. Access credentials are stored in a self-hosted, encrypted
				credential vault, never in plain text, and are never transmitted
				anywhere outside calls to eBay's own APIs.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2><span class="num">6</span>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				This policy may be updated as CardProAI's use of eBay's APIs
				changes. The effective date above reflects the most recent revision.
			</p>
		</section>

		<div class="contact">
			<div class="label">Contact</div>
			<a href="mailto:info@csusportscards.com">info@csusportscards.com</a>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</html>
